mantle rm286
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_bettany_bilgehand
title the thunder buttons
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=quiet honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk counts_steps_between_lightning_and_thunder_with_old_buttons
likes oatcakes wrestling new_boots thunder
dislikes gulls haggling
fears a_loose_sole_on_the_turn a_secret_shouted_from_a_rooftop
hopes boots_with_a_pocket_for_buttons a_storm_heard_under_good_tiles
topics weather +0.5 pastimes +0.4 food +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps buttons for counting the quiet after lightning, hides the best one, and looks for a firm footing before a wrestling match.

words
oath! = Cracked buttonhole | Butter on my bootlace
saying! = Keep a button for the quiet | Hear the roof before the sky
blackone = my little black button | the button like burnt cake
blueone = a blue button with a broken rim | my crooked blue one
cuphand = my counting paw | a pawful of buttons
tinring = the empty ring of a tin | a little tin rattle
thumblip = a raised button edge | a nick under my thumb
oatbit = a burnt oat corner | a crisp oat crumb
laces = two new laces | a matched pair of laces
thunderfoot = a big slow thump | the last far rumble
stairgap = a pause at the turn | the little rest between landings
flatrock = a smooth wrestling stone | my stone for marking the edge

any
opinion festivals for 1 : I like a sweet that takes a long time to suck. Music lasts much longer when the sweet does.
opinion houses against 2 : All that room in a great carriage, and the wheels still throw mud on those of us by the wall.
opinion dole for 2 : A scoop you can smell on the way home is a scoop somebody will be glad to eat.
opinion strangers against 1 : I like to know a voice before I put a good button under a stranger's nose.
opinion church for 1 : The bread goes round under a roof beyond the rain. My ears hear much better when the wet's out of them.

grown

grown
line greet : My buttons have quit knocking. I can hear you now.
line greet.return : I've a quiet word to send back.
line farewell.return : I'll see that my laces are snug before I follow.
line farewell : Find an evening where the roof keeps its word.
line react.news : Let me put that where I can give it some thought.
line react.news.doubt : Did somebody hear it past the first rumble?
line ask.how : Are you feeling steady on your feet?
line thank : Thanks for this inch of dry ground under my toes.

adolescent
line greet : Hold a space at the turn. I can listen.
line greet.return : Heard you. Only counting under my breath.
line farewell.return : I'll take the way with fewer elbows.
line react.news : I might know more after I've heard the far end.
line decline : I'd like to keep some of my pockets to myself.

young
line greet : I'm here. Don't tread on the blue one. | There's a dry step free beside me.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You can speak, but I keep the tin.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : I heard the roof waking up. Hullo.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : It's dark enough to spot the sky flash now.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come close. You can count out of my paw.
line again.open : You went round and came back before the buttons moved.
line greet.return : Hullo. You're louder than a button.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I know you, even with my head down counting.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I heard a voice where my eyes couldn't find a nose.
line farewell : Good walking. Save a step for the thunder.
line farewell.return : I'll finish this count on my own.
line react.news : Wait. I want the news in one ear without a tin rattling in the other.
line react.news.new : I need another button for that bit!
line react.news.known : I had that scrap folded away already.
line react.news.doubt : Did you actually see with your own two eyes?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd give my dry step to a wolf who needed one.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Oh, I could leap three whole treads.
line answer.how : Happy enough. A full pocket sounds nice when I run.
line ask.how : Have you got room in your head for a little game?
line sympathise : I can sit on the other end till you want to talk.
line reassure : I'll hold your place and won't peek.
line decline : I won't show you that pocket. It's where private bits live.
line accept_decline : I'll look up at the roof instead.
line thank : That bit went better with you beside me.
line deflect_thanks : You can give the next loose button to somebody smaller.
line preclose : I want to catch the sound before it rolls away.
line accept_preclose : You go first. I'll start my count again.
line ack : Counted it.

young

scene swap
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : See #blackone#? It buys a turn at my game. | One button has a nick so I know it without looking.
b : Can I give it back? | Why not open your eyes?
a : Yes. You buy your turn, then I buy mine back. Neither of us goes home poorer. | Looking is the easy game. Eyes shut is the extra bit.

scene light
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the sky flashes I start sliding buttons across, singly. | A little roll comes late after a big flash.
b : Till the bang comes? | Does late mean quiet?
a : Yes. Both paws full means the thunder took its time coming. | Not always. That's why I play from under a roof.

scene oats
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put the butter in one hollow in my oatcake. | I've got a little oat crumb on my lip.
b : Why not spread it out? | Are you saving it?
a : So the last bite has a whole pond in the middle. | I'm deciding if I can reach it with my tongue. Paws would be cheating.

scene ring
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put my two buttons down for the ends of a wrestling ring. | I like wrestling on dry ground best.
b : Only two ends to a ring? | Can't you land softer on mud?
a : You have to imagine the bends. I'm saving for more buttons. | Mud keeps hold of a boot when I try to stand up. Then mud has won.

scene newboots
when topic=home self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New boots sound hollow till there are feet inside. | I want a little pocket on each boot.
b : What sound do they make with feet? | Wouldn't you have to bend to reach?
a : The sound I've been wanting. Two thumps at once if I'm quick down a step. | I'd only put spare buttons there. Bending is what makes them spare.

scene gull
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull would pinch my best blue button if it thought the button was a fish eye. | I shut my tin when a gull comes close.
b : Does it look like an eye? | Can the gull get the lid undone?
a : Two holes, so it can't be an eye. A gull's sums are a different question. | Not with a beak. It can knock the whole open tin over, though.

scene secret
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've got one thing in my pocket I don't show. | There's a different rule for telling a secret and telling a story.
b : What does it feel like? | What rule?
a : Like mine. You can feel the outside of the pocket and guess. | A story's allowed to get out and go walking. I shut my fist round a secret.

scene teacher
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw my sums in little pairs of holes. | Counting buttons at lessons makes a smaller noise than counting on a tin.
b : Like a button? | Do you count with the tin too?
a : Exactly. Three pairs are easier to see than six dots skipping all over my page. | Once. The lesson came to a very sudden stop.

scene stairs
when topic=land self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I run the Sump steps in pairs till I get to the cracked one. | There's a bit of wall I tap coming down.
b : Do you skip the crack? | For luck?
a : I do one proper small step on each side. That's a pair too. | So I know to slow down. The landing's right under it.

scene butter
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can draw a weather picture in soft butter. | A slice of bread holds still better than a cloud.
b : Won't somebody eat it? | What do they have in common?
a : I hope so. It's a storm with everything there is for my tea underneath it. | Put butter on the bread, draw cloud shapes, and you can eat the bit of sky you like.

scene drytin
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : You can hear if the tin has got a gap in the lid. | My tin has a little cloth cushion underneath all the buttons.
b : What makes the noise? | To wipe rain out?
a : Drops. Inside drops sound smaller than the ones on top. | No, so the buttons don't all shout together when I'm sneaking by.

scene festivalbit
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sweet wrapper could make a nice kite for a button wolf. | I keep a wrapper folded the same size as two joined buttons.
b : How does the wolf hold on? | Why that size?
a : Through the holes, obviously. String fits better than paws on a button wolf. | It opens into a little tent. My buttons do like a festival out of the wet.

scene hateprices
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If the price is one button it had better still be one button when I pay. | A game stops being a game if the prize keeps moving.
b : What if the prize gets bigger? | Would you walk away?
a : Then it wasn't the prize I was playing for. I like to know beforehand. | I'd put my own prize back in my tin and play counting thunder. The sky never asks for extra.

scene noiseroof
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell a drop on the sill from one on the tin. | I made a little roof with my two paws.
b : What does each one sound like? | What could go under it?
a : One goes tick. One answers back in a larger voice. | My nose gets in. The ears have to mind the weather for themselves.

scene mightsnow
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In my best storm the thunder is all different sizes of button hitting a floor. | Imagine watching a flash run up the sky for a change.
b : Who picks the buttons up? | Wouldn't you be scared?
a : No idea. I only dream as far as playing in the pile. | From under a really thick roof I'd be nearly just curious.

scene clasp
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can make a whole row of faces with holes for eyes. | Some buttons look up even if you turn them over.
b : What about mouths? | Can you make them look down?
a : That one's a scratch. The rest are listening very carefully. | If I put the holey side down nobody sees where the eyes went.

scene feet
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I have to jump I look where both feet will go. | Sometimes I pretend the ground is wrestling me back.
b : Why both? | Who wins that one?
a : Because if I only look for my left foot the right goes looking for its own adventure. | The ground. It never once has to get up afterwards.

adolescent

scene youngertin
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My button tin is getting too small for the old game. | I've learnt to hear the far end of thunder without counting aloud.
b : Too many buttons now? | Have you given up keeping count?
a : Longer fingers. I can hardly get a pinch of small ones out. | Not a chance. I just don't need the street to count along.

scene schoolrace
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can time the walk to a lesson by the echo under one roof. | I'm slower down a stair than I was as a pup.
b : Is the echo always there? | Are your feet less sure?
a : If there's rain. In fair weather I use my perfectly ordinary legs. | They're bigger. I won't land an adult foot in the space a little one used to fit.

scene pockets
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want boots that will carry my little tin a fair distance. | I'd thread a blue button onto one bootlace for a long walk.
b : The boots carry the tin? | As a sign?
a : Through me. I'd like to see another roof my tin sounds good under. | To remind me which lace likes to come untied. Less glamorous than a sign, more useful.

grown

scene fasteners
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep usable fastenings even after the cloth goes. | This old blue button outlasted the pocket it lived in.
b : Where do you keep the scraps? | Did you make another pocket?
a : In a tin that gives a different rattle each year. | Yes, with room to spare. I left the old wear marks where I could see them.

scene likeboots
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wear a new boot round the room before I give it the street. | Laces that look the same sometimes pull quite differently.
b : Will one room tell you much? | How do you tell?
a : Enough to feel the rub before it's too far home to take it off. | Draw them up in separate paws. One will tell you if it's beginning to give.

scene stormwait
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the hush before thunder comes rolling up. | I can find the last note of a storm long after it starts to die.
b : With numbers? | What sound does it finish with?
a : With buttons. A habit's worth keeping when it still gives pleasure. | The little roll too low to hear with much else going on.

scene sumpentry
when topic=land self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Water runs off a Sump step in two streams if there's a chip in the middle. | I have one sightline through the eaves for watching a storm.
b : Does that make a step safer? | Wouldn't a rooftop give a better view?
a : Not a bit. It tells me which edge is still dry to stand on. | Yes. I'd miss the good thick roof. Storms sound better with timber overhead.

scene oatpress
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I press a spoonful of oats quite flat before turning the cake. | The irregular oatcake always looks largest on my plate.
b : Does it make a crisper edge? | Do you pick it for that?
a : Yes. A little soft butter sits very well against the crisp part. | I pick it for the corners, which take more colour from the pan.

scene measure
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fistful of buttons makes a decent grip exercise. | My fingers know the feel of each old button.
b : Don't they press into your paw? | Even the smooth ones?
a : If I squeeze too hard. The whole point's to learn when there's enough grip. | The smooth blanks are as familiar to me as the notches.

scene tidytin
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I line a tin with old cloth so it doesn't announce me everywhere. | The lid has a paper seal to keep little buttons in.
b : Does that spoil the sound? | How do you open it?
a : I lift the cloth when I want the sound. Now the choice is mine. | One slip of paper bends back like a tab. A light thumb is quite enough.

scene askonce
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to ask exactly once before I declare somebody's business public. | A rumour makes a poor fastener for a fact.
b : What answer are you hoping for? | How would you mend the join?
a : The one the owner cares to give. Silence holds just as well. | By leaving the two in separate boxes until there's a real reason to join them.

scene slipfoot
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a wrestling ring drawn big enough for two decent steps of retreat. | When one foot slips I'd sooner put an end to the bout.
b : What if somebody steps out? | Who decides?
a : Then both can start again without anybody getting a side full of stones. | The wolf whose footing slipped. A poor sport would decide for somebody else.

scene rainprice
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a cheap coat's fastenings between my pads. | A loose button costs more time than it looks.
b : Can you find much out like that? | How much time?
a : Sometimes the first coatful of rain will draw the thread right through. I'd sooner test in a dry shop. | However many afternoons I spend hunting its twin once the original's slipped down a gutter.

scene viewfriend
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sometimes dream a tin has just one button too many to close. | My old dream roof has a window for watching the weather.
b : Which button do you give away? | What keeps the rain out?
a : I'd rather find another tin. Some things don't have to stand for a choice. | In the dream, my wish. In the waking world I'd ask for glass.

scene lightfoot
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose the pale stones when the lane gets dim. | Towards dusk the scratches on a black button vanish first.
b : Are the pale stones any less slippery? | Can you still count with it?
a : No. Easier to see the bad places where the edge has gone. | My finger finds the cut even when my eye won't follow.

young

story runoff [topic=weather self.likes=thunder]
  : I put my tin by the door to catch the thunder sound.
  : A drip struck the lid and every loose button jumped at once.
  b : Which button jumped the highest?
  : The one already on top. That's how I discovered you should start a race on a flat floor.

story blueeye [topic=memories]
  : I drew a little wolf in dust and gave it blue buttons for eyes.
  : Wind came along and blew the dust away. Two blue eyes stared straight out of the bare ground.
  b : Was that a bit frightening?
  : Only till I put them in the tin. You get used to a pocket wanting to see out.

story bentcake [topic=food]
  : My oatcake bent before I could grab the edge, so all its butter went into a valley.
  : I tore the cake straight down both ends of the valley and rolled it up.
  b : And the butter stayed put?
  : Till I took the first bite. I had a very buttery nose and no regrets.

young

rule @tin
when concept=bark self.likes=thunder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Quiet tin, sky coming through! | That's a two-button rumble.

rule @boots
when concept=bark self.likes=new_boots
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Don't stand where my right foot's going! | Two steps for a new pair.

rule @gull
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lid on, gull above! | My blue one's no fish eye.

rule @cake
when concept=bark self.likes=oatcakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Save me the wrinkly edge. | Butter fits in that hollow!

young
dlg resident.hub : You can stand by my tin if you keep both feet still.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Oh, #topic.player#. You may see the blue one.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : There's room by the wall. My tin stays shut.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Are your ears awake? Mine are, even in the dark.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I can count soft things and loud things now.
dlg resident.job : I've a private bit of sorting on my paws.
dlg resident.bye : I'll hear your feet till you get round the bend.

young

graft @button_rumble resident.hub
choice What are those buttons counting? -> button_rumble
node button_rumble
say The quiet before the thunder. Look, I put a black one here and move a blue one across for every beat. You can try it if you promise not to rush the blue.
choice How do I know when it's finished? -> button_rumble_more
choice Put the lid down gently. -> hub
node button_rumble_more
say The sky finishes it. If the tin goes bang first, that's you dropping the lid and we have to start the whole game again.
choice Put the lid down gently. -> hub
choice Leave the little tin alone. -> bye
